momenta `k₁, k₂, L`, one external momentum `p` with `p² = -1` (the electron on shell, mass `1`),
and the nine denominators

* `D₁ = k₁²`, `D₂ = k₂²`, `D₃ = (k₁ + k₂)²` (photons);
* `D₄ = (p - k₁)² + 1`, `D₅ = (p - k₁ - k₂)² + 1` (the open electron line);
* `D₆ = L² + 1`, `D₇ = (L + k₁)² + 1`, `D₈ = (L + k₁ + k₂)² + 1` (the closed electron loop);
* `D₉ = (L + p)²`

`D₉` is an irreducible numerator. An index vector `ν` stands for `∫ ∏ D_a^{-ν_a}`. With
Minkowski denominators `q² - m²` and `p² = 1` (as in Kira) the integrals are `(-1)^{Σ ν}` times
these, up to a factor independent of `ν`. The data (`quad`, `const`) encode `D_a` as a quadratic
form in `(k₁, k₂, L, p)` plus a constant; `tmpl` is the IBP template, checked against the data by
`QED.Algebra.IBPCert.Family.tmplOk`, and `zeroSectors` are the scaleless sectors (Lee's
criterion, computed offline).

